## Configuring Search

### Search Type

Set `search_type` to `"fast"` to run each `web_search` call on the lower-latency Fast Search path. Fast calls cost \$1.00 per 1,000 invocations instead of \$2.50, plus model tokens. Set `search_type` to `"web"` for standard web search. If you omit it, the tool inherits the effort level's search type when one is configured; otherwise, it uses `"web"`.

Use `fast` for day-to-day agent loops and high-volume tool calls. Use `web` for rare, difficult, or ambiguous questions. `search_type` is separate from the Agent API [`fast` effort level](https://docs.perplexity.ai/docs/agent-api/effort).

The `fast`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, and `xhigh` [effort levels](https://docs.perplexity.ai/docs/agent-api/effort.md) set `search_type: "fast"` by default. To override an effort level's search type, pass `search_type` on the `web_search` tool in your request.

First, [install a library and set `PERPLEXITY_API_KEY`](https://docs.perplexity.ai/docs/agent-api/quickstart). Passing `search_type` on the `web_search` tool requires Perplexity Python library 0.43.6 or later, or TypeScript SDK 0.38.6 or later. Older TypeScript SDK versions fail type checking on this field. If you can't upgrade, cast the tool object with `as any`.

```python Python theme={null}
from perplexity import Perplexity

client = Perplexity()

response = client.responses.create(
    model="openai/gpt-5.6-luna",
    input="What is the latest stable Rust release, and what changed?",
    tools=[
        {
            "type": "web_search",
            "search_type": "fast"
        }
    ]
)

print(response.output_text)
```

