# Perplexity Search API

> Access real-time web search results with Perplexity's Search API. Get ranked results, domain filtering, multi-query search, and content extraction for developers.

## Overview

Perplexity's Search API returns real-time, ranked web results as structured data, with controls for domains, languages, regions, and extracted content.

Use the Search API when you need raw results for your own processing. For an LLM-generated answer with citations, use the [Agent API](https://docs.perplexity.ai/docs/agent-api/quickstart.md).

## Add Perplexity Search to your agent

Ask your agent to install the Perplexity CLI (`pplx`) skill, which searches the web from the terminal:

```text wrap theme={null}
Read https://github.com/perplexityai/api-platform-developers/blob/main/skills/pplx-cli/SKILL.md and install this skill.
```

You can also [try Perplexity Search in the interactive Playground](https://console.perplexity.ai/project/playground/search) with no API key required.

> [!TIP]
>
> You can now run Perplexity Search straight from your terminal.
> The [Perplexity CLI](https://docs.perplexity.ai/docs/cli/overview.md) returns the same ranked results as JSON, ready for shell pipelines and agent tool calls, with no code to write.

### Use these results in your own agent

Search returns ranked results with page text in `snippet`, and no generated answer. Your model reads the text and writes the answer. To call Search as a tool from your own agent loop, follow the guide for your model provider: [OpenAI SDK](https://docs.perplexity.ai/docs/search/agent-sdks/openai.md), [Anthropic SDK](https://docs.perplexity.ai/docs/search/agent-sdks/anthropic.md), or [Gemini SDK](https://docs.perplexity.ai/docs/search/agent-sdks/gemini.md). For Claude Code, Cursor, VS Code, and other MCP clients, add the [Perplexity API MCP server](https://docs.perplexity.ai/docs/getting-started/integrations/mcp-server.md) instead. The result fields, the token budget controls, and how to handle an empty `snippet` are in [Use these results in your own agent](https://docs.perplexity.ai/docs/search/overview.md#use-these-results-in-your-own-agent) on the overview.

## Installation

Install one of our [official SDKs](https://docs.perplexity.ai/docs/sdk/overview.md) for a convenient, type-safe integration:

```bash Python theme={null}
pip install perplexityai
```

```bash Typescript theme={null}
npm install @perplexity-ai/perplexity_ai
```

## Authentication

Set your API key as an environment variable. The official SDKs read it automatically, but you can also pass it explicitly:

> [tab] macOS/Linux
>
> ```bash theme={null}
> export PERPLEXITY_API_KEY="your_api_key_here"
> ```

> [tab] Windows
>
> ```powershell theme={null}
> setx PERPLEXITY_API_KEY "your_api_key_here"
> ```

Confirm the key is set without printing it:

> [tab] macOS/Linux
>
> ```bash theme={null}
> test -n "$PERPLEXITY_API_KEY" && echo "PERPLEXITY_API_KEY is set" || echo "PERPLEXITY_API_KEY is not set"
> ```

> [tab] Windows
>
> ```powershell theme={null}
> if ($env:PERPLEXITY_API_KEY) { "PERPLEXITY_API_KEY is set" } else { "PERPLEXITY_API_KEY is not set" }
> ```

> [!WARNING]
>
> Never print the key or any part of it. Commands like `env`, `echo $PERPLEXITY_API_KEY`, or a prefix or length check leave the key in shell history, logs, and coding-agent transcripts. Read the key from the environment in code and tests, and don't paste it into fixtures or commit messages.

## Basic Usage

Start with a basic search query to get relevant web results. `max_results` accepts values from 1 to 20 and defaults to 10. See the [API Reference](https://docs.perplexity.ai/api-reference/search-post.md) for all parameters and [pricing](https://docs.perplexity.ai/docs/getting-started/pricing.md) for search costs.

> [!NOTE]
>
> The Search API request has one endpoint, `POST https://api.perplexity.ai/search`, and only the parameters in the [API reference](https://docs.perplexity.ai/api-reference/search-post.md). Agent API fields such as `model`, `effort`, `instructions`, `tools`, and `max_output_tokens` are not part of a search request. The response is ranked results with titles, URLs, and extracted text; there is no generated answer. To have a model read the results, pass them to your own model or call the [Agent API](https://docs.perplexity.ai/docs/agent-api/quickstart.md) with the `web_search` tool instead.

```python Python theme={null}
from perplexity import Perplexity

client = Perplexity()

search = client.search.create(
    query="GPT-5.5 release announcement details",
    max_results=5
)

for result in search.results:
    print(f"{result.title}: {result.url}")
```

```typescript Typescript theme={null}
import Perplexity from '@perplexity-ai/perplexity_ai';

const client = new Perplexity();

const search = await client.search.create({
    query: "GPT-5.5 release announcement details",
    max_results: 5
});

for (const result of search.results) {
    console.log(`${result.title}: ${result.url}`);
}
```

